Depending on the metallicity and other model assumptions, population synthesis studies by Dominik et al. (2012)5 predict average BH masses of 8-10 M_{\\odot}, roughly consistent with observations (McClintock et al., 2013). For simplicity and independence of additional modeling assumptions (like delay-time distribution and metallicity evolution), we consider only the time-averaged merger rate over the Galactic history. We exclude binaries with lifetimes exceeding the age of the Galaxy and checked that our estimates do not depend significantly on the lifetimes of the merging systems. Our constraints yield firm upper limits of the present-day NS-BH merger rate.

